  "notes": [
    "CAMPAIGN.md §9.1 / §12.2 '5-1'..'5-6'; areas a0 = S1 (outside, night), a1 = S2-S3, a2 = S4-S6.",
    "KI1: E7a2 336-448 is a mesh door and a ramp (no floor at 320-368), so the copied stacks are E7a2 448-960 (a 96-px lane) in 5-2 and 448-960 flip in 5-6.",
    "The hero idle frames behind the tank glass of 5-4 need hero records drawn into the stage page; they are left for the G6 overlay (gap noted in the WP-E report). The E7a3 monitors stay in their ROM state (waveform cells were not identified as dynamic states), never a face: E7a3 1264+ (the monitor wall of the Fessenden reveal) is not used.",
    "Section casts (CAMPAIGN §4.4 'cast', merged over the chapter pool): lighter A/BOMB/KNIFE variants where the ROM-affine HP budget of the chapter's waves exceeded ENEMIES §2.6 by more than 15% (tests/campaign.cjs (8)); ratio now 1.137.",
    "5-4..5-6 re-cut so that joins are mirror joins or sit under a vault post: 5-4 = E8a0 592-1104 (tanks 05-08, all four in the hall since G6 verify r2; never mirrored: a mirrored tank row shows the plate 08 as '80') and E7a3 0-512 flip; 5-5 = E7a3 0-512 and its mirror; 5-6 = E8a0 864-1120, E7a2 448-960 flip, E4a2 512-768 and E4a2 640-768 flip.",
    "Seams (CAMPAIGN §4.1 join chunks): every join that is not a mirror join is covered by a vault post, the chained steel post of the E7a2 archive door (E7a2 400-432, palette row 21 lifted: full height, foreground).",
    "Far layer: one per section; only E5a0, E4a2 and E8a0 have a scroll3 here (5-1 E5a0 night, 5-2 E4a2, 5-4 and 5-6 E8a0); the E7a2 and E7a3 interiors are opaque above the floor.",
    "The coldlab preset washes the interiors out, so a1/a2 add saturation x1.25, lightness x0.82."
  ],
